olved in current events  because he doesn't have the power to be  an asset anymore just a liability  although to be fair there's a lot more  to it than that because it's not like  Gaughan has a strong desire to visit the  Dark Continent so it's not like he's  being excluded from the story it's more  like Gaughan has made the decision to  remove himself from the action but even  if we accept it that yes this is a  shounen manga and the main character  should be involved anyway having him on  an expedition to the Dark Continent  probably isn't you know the wisest of  ideas even if he did still have access  to nen I highly doubt that the hunter  Association would have recruited him for  this mission I mean the people who have  been selected to go to the Dark  Continent are highly skilled incredibly  intelligent or otherwise absurdly  valuable in some way shape or form know  the descriptor of which is really ever  fit gone he is a pretty reckless being  and what has seen him through the series  thus far has been a mixture of natural  talent and the efforts of those around  him to keep him alive one way Gong could  have been integrated into things though  is if after meeting Jing he decided to  stay with him and became a part of the  beyond networ faction and headed to the  Dark Continent that way  however the manga did address the idea  of why gone did not choose to stay with  Jing and he himself said that if he'd  had access to aura then he would have  loved to travel with his father but at  the same time after completing his goal  of meeting him gone realized that Jing  wasn't really a father more like a cool  uncle and without access to aura there  was really no reason to stay with him  because he had other priorities in life  and this is very much the crux of why  gun is not involved in current events  the fact of the matter is that GaN  started this series but the simple goal  of finding Jing and  accomplish that goal it cost him  everything to do serve it he did i